        "problem": "The sales manager of a company that produces wooden furniture analyses the weekly profit made by creating $x$ wooden tables per week. They found that the weekly profit $p(x),$ in dollars, can be modeled by the quadratic function\n\n$$\np(x)=a{x}^{2}+bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants.",
